---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Ask" description="Ask questions grounded in Josef Urban's published work — answered by Premise, the AI host of this archive.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-16 pb-20">
    <p class="text-sm font-mono font-medium text-accent uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Ask</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-medium text-ink mb-4">Ask Premise</h1>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
      <strong class="text-ink">Premise</strong> is the AI host of this archive, named for
      premise selection &mdash; deciding which of thousands of known facts a proof actually
      needs, the bottleneck this record keeps returning to.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Open the host with the widget at the bottom-right of any page. It retrieves
      passages from the papers indexed here and answers from them, with citations.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-8 text-sm">
      Premise is not Josef Urban and does not speak for him. It is grounded in his
      published work and nothing else; when the corpus does not cover a question, it
      should say so rather than invent an answer.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/corpus/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-accent text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-md text-sm font-medium hover:bg-accent-mid transition-colors">
        Browse the corpus
      </a>
      <a href="/dictionary/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-surface border border-border text-ink px-5 py-2.5 rounded-md text-sm font-medium hover:border-accent/40 transition-colors">
        Dictionary
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
